          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A factory produces 25 widgets in 4 minutes. Each widget requires 15 g of plastic.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Plastic costs $3.20 per kg. What is the cost per hour, in dollars?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{\\$18}{\\text{h}}$",
      "worked": "$w$ denotes widgets.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\text{cost}}{\\text{time}}&=\\frac{\\text{widgets}}{\\text{time}}\\times\\frac{\\text{plastic}}{\\text{widget}}\\times\\frac{\\text{cost}}{\\text{plastic}}\\\\\n\\frac{\\$x}{1\\text{ hour}}&=\\frac{25\\text{ w}}{4\\text{ min}}\\times\\frac{15\\text{ g}}{1\\text{ w}}\\times\\frac{\\$3.20}{1\\text{ kg}}\\\\\n\\frac{\\$x}{1\\text{ hour}}&=\\frac{25\\text{ w}}{(4\\div60)\\text{ h}}\\times\\frac{(15\\div1000)\\text{ kg}}{1\\text{ w}}\\times\\frac{\\$3.20}{1\\text{ kg}}\\\\\nx&=18\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe cost is $\\frac{\\$18}{\\text{h}}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
